WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.079 --> 00:00:02.841
SoilWorkspace provides an integrated workflow—

2
00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:07.525
preparing reliable material models from
experimental data for field-scale simulation.

3
00:00:07.855 --> 00:00:10.242
It has three main hubs: the Experimental Hub,

4
00:00:10.449 --> 00:00:12.329
the Calibration Hub, and the Modeling Hub—

5
00:00:12.794 --> 00:00:14.281
each with dedicated workspaces.

6
00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:18.461
The Experimental Hub brings soil characterization into one place.

7
00:00:18.795 --> 00:00:24.738
Material Classification combines particle-size distributions and index
properties to determine soil classification.

8
00:00:25.147 --> 00:00:28.288
Single Test Analysis interprets individual experiments.

9
00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:33.175
For example, it identifies compression and swelling indices from the
oedometer test shown here.

10
00:00:33.645 --> 00:00:36.300
Batch Test Analysis reveals material-level relationships,

11
00:00:36.602 --> 00:00:39.176
including critical state and undrained instability.

12
00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:43.712
The Calibration Hub connects experimental
insights with advanced constitutive models.

13
00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:49.115
Automatic calibration fits selected parameters to
measured responses within defined bounds.

14
00:00:49.653 --> 00:00:53.816
Fit Assessment quantifies the agreement and
highlights the remaining differences.

15
00:00:54.338 --> 00:00:58.834
The Modeling Hub explores predicted behavior across a variety of stress
paths through triaxial,

16
00:00:59.053 --> 00:01:01.695
biaxial, simple-shear, and hollow-cylinder tests.

17
00:01:02.146 --> 00:01:07.108
The undrained biaxial response shown here
illustrates this numerical testing capability.

18
00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:13.272
Its platform-specific user-defined model generator bridges material
modelling and field-scale analysis.

19
00:01:13.594 --> 00:01:15.193
PLAXIS is the example shown here.

20
00:01:15.525 --> 00:01:20.352
SoilWorkspace prepares the model; external
platforms run the field-scale analysis.

21
00:01:20.706 --> 00:01:26.537
SoilWorkspace: one place to turn raw data into a
robust material model for engineering analysis.

22
00:01:26.821 --> 00:01:28.314
Currently under active development.

23
00:01:28.661 --> 00:01:29.776
Keep an eye out for the release!
